# Byte-exact checkout, everywhere.
#
# Every result record carries a SHA-256 of the data it ran on, and each card.json
# stores a hash over its meta.csv. Git's default end-of-line conversion on Windows
# rewrites LF as CRLF on checkout, which changes those bytes and makes the
# card-vs-live-data assertion fail on a fresh clone while the files are, logically,
# identical. `-text` disables all EOL conversion and content sniffing, so a clone is
# a byte copy of what was committed, on every platform.
* -text
